content.text:
The "All products" and "Bundles" headings on the products page are now uppercase, 16px, with 0.08em letter spacing. The 16 functional tests pass. I didn't load the page in a browser to check how it looks.

The change is a new rule in `site/css/pages.css`, under the Products block:

```css
.page-products .section-title {
  font-size: 16px;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
}
```

`.section-title` is also used on the home, about, pricing and orders pages. I scoped the rule to `.page-products` so those pages keep their current headings. The 16px size also holds on small screens, because the mobile `h2` rule (21px) doesn't override a class selector.

STATUS: DONE

